{"abstract":"Dette kapitel har fokus på: - Forskellen mellem motion, idræt og fysisk aktivitet - Borgere med autismes fysiske aktivitetsniveau og idrætsdeltagelse - Barrierer for motion og idræt - Tilpasset tilrettelæggelse af motions- og idrætsaktiviteter","author_count":3,"contributors":["Bentholm, Anette"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-715148"],"filters":{"added":"2024-02","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Autisme","Idræt","Motion"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-UC"],"level3":{"UC":["DI-UC-ALL","DI-UC-UCN"]},"level3all":["DI-UC-UCN"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"motion og idræt","src":["ucn"],"src-code":["DI-UC-UCN"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://gad.dk/praksisbog-om-autisme-for-ergo-og-fysioterapeuter","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-715148","ids":["ucn-9f4c8d77-f7f9-4ff5-9122-1d137f5ebaec"],"keyword":["autisme","idræt","motion"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-B51D7BBCAF1A952CE341DDF2C8C2477B"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ucn university college of northern denmark","l2":"DI-UC","l2n":"University Colleges","l3":"DI-UC-UCN","l3nl":"University College of Northern Denmark","l3nn":"UCN University College of Northern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"UCN University College of Northern Denmark","namevar":["Professionshøjskolen UCN, UCN Direktion, Forskningscenter for In- og eksklusion i pædagogisk praksis","Professionshøjskolen UCN, UCN Direktion, UCN Velfærd, Pædagoguddannelsen Hjørring"],"nora_code":"DI-UC-UCN","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anette","key":"bentholmpau","last":"Bentholm","locid":"6b1b9184-84df-405c-978c-17e2b3e92ffe","name":"Bentholm, Anette","orcid":"0000-0001-8578-0429","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Diana","key":"astrupnielsenpedh","last":"Astrup Nielsen","name":"Astrup Nielsen, Diana","rank":2,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Kirsten","key":"bundgaardpedh","last":"Bundgaard","name":"Bundgaard, Kirsten","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"isbn":["9788712069485"],"pages":"139-151","publisher":"Gad","status":"p","title":"Praksisbog om autisme for ergo- og fysioterapeuter"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All University Colleges","DI-ALL","DI-UC","DI-UC-ALL","University College of Northern Denmark","University Colleges"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ucn-9f4c8d77-f7f9-4ff5-9122-1d137f5ebaec"],"src":["UCN University College of Northern Denmark"],"title":"Motion og idræt","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-715148","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Chemoradiotherapy (CRT) may induce myocardial dysfunction, congestive heart failure, and impaired physical performance in patients with esophageal cancer (EC). We aimed to investigate left ventricular (LV) function at rest and during stress, using echocardiography (echo) and a cardiopulmonary exercise (CPX) test both before and immediately after completing CRT. MATERIAL AND METHODS: Consecutive EC patients referred for curative treatment were enrolled. Patients attended either definitive CRT or neoadjuvant CRT with subsequent surgery. The evaluation included cardiac biomarkers, electrocardiogram, echo, and CPX test. The primary endpoint was changes in left ventricular (LV) global longitudinal strain (GLS) at rest. Secondary endpoints were LV ejection fraction (LVEF), LV diastolic function, LVEF and GLS at peak exercise, and maximal oxygen consumption (VO2max). The trial was registered with ClinicalTrials.gov (NCT03619317). RESULTS: Among 47 patients enrolled (94% male; median age 67 years, range 50-86 years), cardiac examinations were performed a median of three days [Interquartile range (IQR (1-5))] before CRT and one day [IQR (0-6)] after CRT. At rest, GLS and LVEF decreased, 17.6 vs. 16.4% and 56.4 vs. 55.1%, respectively (p = 0.004; p = 0.030). Furthermore, an absolute decrease of at least 5% in LVEF and 2.5% in GLS was noted in 21% of the patients. Signs of LV diastolic dysfunction increased from 13 to 21% (p = ns). VO2max significantly decreased; 21.2 ml/kg/min vs. 18.8 ml/kg/min (p < 0.001). CONCLUSION: LV function and physical performance decreased in EC patients after CRT, and the LV systolic reserve capacity declined. This study highlighted that EC treatment was associated with early cardiac side effects, which may have clinical and prognostic implications.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Astrup Søndergaard, Mette Marie","Nordsmark, Marianne","Møller, Ditte Sloth","Nielsen, Kirsten Melgaard","Poulsen, Steen Hvitfeldt"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-194570"],"filters":{"added":"2022-04","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Cardiac function","Cardiotoxicity","Chemoradiotherapy","Esophageal cancer","Working capacity"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"reduction in myocardial function and oxygen consumption after chemoradiotherapy in patients with esophageal cancer","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85126708800","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-194570","identifier":[{"id":"000769246600001","type":"wos"},{"id":"85126708800","type":"scopus"},{"id":"35289694","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-724035da-f283-4b34-b5a0-e52401abab6b"],"keyword":["Esophageal cancer","cardiac function","cardiotoxicity","chemoradiotherapy","working capacity"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-2D595642610045FD5060A772022145AD"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - The Department of Cardiological Medicine B"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mette Marie","key":"astrupsøndergaardpau","last":"Astrup Søndergaard","locid":"06a52faa-a291-4e16-b79b-598f62d06a37","name":"Astrup Søndergaard, Mette Marie","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Marianne","key":"nordsmarkpau","last":"Nordsmark","locid":"bf7f673d-6979-4263-b3c4-7ac31e6ab035","name":"Nordsmark, Marianne","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ditte","key":"slothmøllerpau","last":"Sloth Møller","locid":"a12cd26d-0f14-4586-a270-9f0667193396","name":"Møller, Ditte Sloth","name_org":"Sloth Møller, Ditte","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Kirsten","key":"melgaardnielsenpau","last":"Melgaard Nielsen","locid":"6cefe1c5-8444-4edf-a360-312ed8875629","name":"Nielsen, Kirsten Melgaard","name_org":"Melgaard Nielsen, Kirsten","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Steen Hvitfeldt","key":"poulsenpau","last":"Poulsen","locid":"ec1d0fd4-f6ae-4071-907f-1448dfe832fe","name":"Poulsen, Steen Hvitfeldt","orcid":"0000-0002-9586-835X","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["35289694"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1080/0284186x.2022.2048068","issn":["0284186X","11001704"],"issn_org":["0284186X"],"issue":"5","journal":"Acta Oncologica","pages":"566-574","publisher":"Medical Journals Sweden AB","status":"p","title":"Acta Oncologica","volume":"61"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85126708800"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-724035da-f283-4b34-b5a0-e52401abab6b"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Reduction in myocardial function and oxygen consumption after chemoradiotherapy in patients with esophageal cancer","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-194570","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"AIM: The aim was to identify the prevalence of long-lasting pain among children with cerebral palsy (CP) and to investigate the association between pain and participation in physical leisure activities. METHODS: This is a cross-sectional study based on data from the National Danish Clinical Quality Database of children with CP. The study population consisted of 960 children aged 2-11 years across all Gross Motor Function Classification System (GMFCS) levels. Data were collected at children's regular clinical visits in 2016 or 2017. Information about pain and participation in physical leisure activities were obtained. The association was estimated as odds ratios (OR) and 95% confidence intervals (95% CI) by logistic regression adjusted for age and sex. RESULTS: We included data from 817 children (59% boys) median age six years, 52% classified as GMFCS-level I. A total of 36% reported pain and the most frequent pain locations were hips, feet and knees. Children reporting pain had lower odds for participation in physical leisure activities (OR 0.71, 95% CI 0.53-0.96). CONCLUSION: A large proportion of children with CP reported pain. There is an indication that long-lasting pain influences participation in physical leisure activities. Pain relieving interventions are important to decrease pain-related suffering and facilitate participation.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Østergaard, Cecilie Schmidt","Pedersen, Nanna Sofie Astrup","Thomasen, Anne","Mechlenburg, Inger","Nordbye-Nielsen, Kirsten"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-230405"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Østergaard, Cecilie Schmidt"],"keyword":["Cerebral palsy","Children","Pain","Participation"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"pain is frequent in children with cerebral palsy and negatively affects physical activity and participation","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85085568770","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-230405","identifier":[{"id":"000535307900001","type":"wos"},{"id":"85085568770","type":"scopus"},{"id":"32374451","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-b132fb43-558f-4206-9853-7b5b70075552"],"keyword":["cerebral palsy","children","pain","participation","physical leisure activity"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-B40608E3B29867C65CEA95024B54D119"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Orthopaedic surgery"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Unspecified organisation"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Cecilie Schmidt","key":"østergaardpau","last":"Østergaard","locid":"f9923090-db9f-4c63-808e-e0ccd525b18c","name":"Østergaard, Cecilie Schmidt","orcid":"0000-0001-8459-8350","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Nanna Sofie Astrup","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"7ab7c723-e60c-4277-9d97-2f39bca5b0a3","name":"Pedersen, Nanna Sofie Astrup","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anne","key":"thomasenpau","last":"Thomasen","locid":"a93621e2-f77e-4800-876c-647090dc6806","name":"Thomasen, Anne","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Inger","key":"mechlenburgpau","last":"Mechlenburg","locid":"b46c351d-ea23-4836-8426-a5402fd1a2bd","name":"Mechlenburg, Inger","orcid":"0000-0001-5432-8691","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Kirsten","key":"nordbyenielsenpau","last":"Nordbye-Nielsen","locid":"7c30dc04-e6e9-4c7c-bb6c-69020f71b76f","name":"Nordbye-Nielsen, Kirsten","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["32374451"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/apa.15341","issn":["08035253","08035326"],"issn_org":["08035253"],"issue":"1","journal":"Acta Paediatrica","pages":"301-306","publisher":"Wiley-Blackwell","status":"p","title":"Acta Paediatrica","volume":"110"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85085568770"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-b132fb43-558f-4206-9853-7b5b70075552"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Pain is frequent in children with cerebral palsy and negatively affects physical activity and participation","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-230405","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Objectives: The aim of this study was to characterize the cardiovascular disease (CVD) profile and describe the incidence and characteristics of cardiovascular (CV) events in patients with esophageal cancer (EC) following chemoradiation and surgery. Background: Underlying CVD is a concern in patients with EC receiving curative treatment with chemoradiation and surgery. Methods: Consecutive patients with EC referred for curative treatment were enrolled. Clinical CVD status, ongoing CVD treatment, cardiac function, and physical performance were assessed before chemoradiation. During a 90-day follow-up period, all CV events were noted and classified after in-depth medical record review. CV events were defined by major adverse CV events (transient ischemic attack, imaging-verified new stroke, unstable angina, heart failure or cardiomyopathy) or by Common Terminology Criteria for Adverse Events grade ≥3 (arrhythmia, thromboembolic events, or pericardial effusion requiring pericardiocentesis). Results: Among 55 patients enrolled (median age 67 years; range: 50-86 years; 89% men), 22% had CVD prior to chemoradiation, and 11% with pre-existing CVD were inadequately treated according to current CV guidelines. Thirteen patients (24%) developed 15 events during follow-up. Pre-existing atrial fibrillation and a dilated left atrium were significantly associated with subsequent CV events. Left ventricular (LV) systolic dysfunction was frequently noted; 51% had impaired LV global longitudinal strain (<18%), and 16% had LV ejection fraction <50%. Conclusions: A systematic cardiac evaluation prior to chemoradiation in patients with EC revealed a high prevalence of undetected CVD, inadequately treated pre-existing CVD, and a high incidence of CV events after chemoradiation. These findings highlight the need for a systematic baseline cardiac examination in patients with EC to optimize CVD treatment. (Impact of Cancer Therapy on Myocardial Function in Patients With Esophagus Cancer [Heartcheck]; NCT03619317)","author_count":4,"contributors":["Astrup Søndergaard, Mette Marie","Nordsmark, Marianne","Nielsen, Kirsten Melgaard","Poulsen, Steen Hvitfeldt"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-234618"],"filters":{"added":"2022-03","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Astrup Søndergaard, Mette Marie"],"keyword":["Cardiac function","Cardiovascular disease","Chemoradiation","Esophageal cancer"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"cardiovascular burden and adverse events in patients with esophageal cancer treated with chemoradiation for curative intent","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jaccao.2021.10.002","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-234618","identifier":[{"id":"34988480","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC8702793","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85120860912","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-b88789e8-bb38-42d3-8f76-ff0df86d9b5c"],"keyword":["cardiac function","cardiovascular disease","chemoradiation","esophageal cancer"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-B6C25DAAC43324E53B6D4B904363C20A"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jaccao.2021.10.002","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - The Department of Cardiological Medicine B"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mette Marie A.","key":"søndergaardpau","last":"Søndergaard","locid":"06a52faa-a291-4e16-b79b-598f62d06a37","name":"Astrup Søndergaard, Mette Marie","name_org":"Søndergaard, Mette Marie A.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Marianne","key":"nordsmarkpau","last":"Nordsmark","locid":"bf7f673d-6979-4263-b3c4-7ac31e6ab035","name":"Nordsmark, Marianne","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Kirsten M.","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"6cefe1c5-8444-4edf-a360-312ed8875629","name":"Nielsen, Kirsten Melgaard","name_org":"Nielsen, Kirsten M.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Steen H.","key":"poulsenpau","last":"Poulsen","locid":"ec1d0fd4-f6ae-4071-907f-1448dfe832fe","name":"Poulsen, Steen Hvitfeldt","name_org":"Poulsen, Steen H.","orcid":"0000-0002-9586-835X","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["34988480"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.jaccao.2021.10.002","issn":["26660873"],"issue":"5","journal":"JACC: CardioOncology","pages":"711-721","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"JACC: CardioOncology","volume":"3"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85120860912"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-b88789e8-bb38-42d3-8f76-ff0df86d9b5c"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Cardiovascular Burden and Adverse Events in Patients With Esophageal Cancer Treated With Chemoradiation for Curative Intent","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-234618","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Evidensbegrebet har længe domineret uddannelsesforskningen. Med John Hatties gennemslagskraft også i dansk uddannelsesvidenskab og –politik er det i tilgift den medicinske videnskabs randomiserede kontrollerede studier (RCT), der udgør den gyldne standard. Tilhængere har imidlertid ikke taget de fulde konsekvenser af denne metode, for hvor bliver spørgsmålet om placeboeffekten af i uddannelsesforskningen? Spørgsmålet stilles, fordi den problemstilling, man beskriver med placeboeffekten, også må være på spil, når man underviser og lærer.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Hyldgaard, Kirsten"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-142783"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Empiri","Evidens","Overføring","Placebo","Psykoanalyse","Spekulation","Uddannelsespolitik","Undervisning"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"pædagogikkens placebo","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-142783","ids":["au-1754c6d0-6f8a-4b5c-9c86-b059a363a5d9"],"keyword":["Dobbeltblindtest","Empiri","Evidens","Overføring","Placebo","Psykoanalyse","Spekulation","Uddannelsespolitik","Undervisning"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Local-1-1-7611905539128DFA0424D84A529F78DC"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Arts, Danish School of Education, Danish School of Education - Education Studies, Emdrup"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Kirsten","key":"hyldgaardpau","last":"Hyldgaard","locid":"6c5ce424-d7b4-473b-944e-ec0effb52ab9","name":"Hyldgaard, Kirsten","orcid":"0000-0003-0647-6731","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Lene","key":"tanggaardpedh","last":"Tanggaard","name":"Tanggaard, Lene","rank":2,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Svend","key":"brinkmannpedh","last":"Brinkmann","name":"Brinkmann, Svend","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Thomas Aastrup","key":"rømerpedh","last":"Rømer","name":"Rømer, Thomas Aastrup","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"isbn":["9788771299991"],"pages":"36-47","place":"Aarhus","publisher":"Klim","status":"p","title":"Uren pædagogik 3"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-1754c6d0-6f8a-4b5c-9c86-b059a363a5d9"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Pædagogikkens placebo?","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-142783","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"Artiklen omhandler arbejdet med et aktionsforskningsinspireret projekt under Program for Realkompetence (NVR). Projektet har fokus på indkredsning og vurdering af ikke-formelle og uformelle kompetencer hos IKV-ansøgere til læreruddannelsen. Hensigten med projektet er at skabe viden om, hvordan man på læreruddannelsen kan kvalitetssikre arbejdet med at forstå og vurdere IKV-ansøgeres samlede kompetencer samt udvikle en fælles tilgang til optagelse af IKV-studerende med henblik på ansøgernes retsstilling. Der arbejdes med at udvikle en interviewguide og vurderingskriterier for de ansøgere, der tilbydes en IKV-samtale. Dette arbejde er inspireret af læringsteori, teori om kompetenceforståelse, konstruktivistisk vejledningsteori samt kommunikationsteori.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Mølgaard, Dorthe Busk","Damkier, Maja","Blaabjerg, Bitten Aastrup"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-049800"],"filters":{"added":"2023-01","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Realkompetencevurdering","Uddannelse professioner og erhverv"],"level":"pop","oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-UC"],"level3":{"UC":["DI-UC-ALL","DI-UC-UCL","DI-UC-VIA"]},"level3all":["DI-UC-UCL","DI-UC-VIA"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"ikv ved læreruddannelsen at forstå og vurdere ikke formelle og uformelle kompetencer hos ikv ansøgere til læreruddannelsen","src":["ucl","via"],"src-code":["DI-UC-UCL","DI-UC-VIA"],"type":"dra","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S02-100.00-049800","ids":["ucl-7347664f-5c29-4c09-9f3f-d55f4c1d5794","via-7347664f-5c29-4c09-9f3f-d55f4c1d5794"],"keyword":["Uddannelse, professioner og erhverv","realkompetencevurdering"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Popular","noi":["Local-1-2-69C250C66160F87F714BB8716ECF9DF4"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"via university college","l2":"DI-UC","l2n":"University Colleges","l3":"DI-UC-VIA","l3nl":"VIA University College","l3nn":"VIA Uni